# Client configuration (F5). Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and adjust as needed.
#
# Base URL of the .NET backend (QaAutomation.Api). Every transport — the axios client, React Query,
# EventSource streams, the Reports iframe/download, the Settings preview window, and the error logger
# — builds URLs from this via src/config/env.ts (apiUrl).
#
# Leave EMPTY for local development: `npm run dev` proxies /api -> http://localhost:5250 (see
# vite.config.ts), and a same-origin reverse proxy / static-host rewrite serves /api in production.
# Set to an absolute origin (no trailing slash) to point a build at a remote backend, e.g.:
#   VITE_QA_API=https://qa-api.example.com
VITE_QA_API=
